{"seq":29,"slug":"database-transactions-concurrency","title":"数据库事务与并发控制","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency","rating":{"composite":3.8,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"数据库事务与并发控制\">数据库事务与并发控制</h1><p>银行从一个账户向另一个账户转账，扣款成功而入账失败，是任何数据库都不能接受的结局。事务正是为了把「要么全做、要么全不做」这件事变成系统的硬保证而存在的抽象。本 hub 围绕一个核心张力展开：单条事务想看到一个安静、独占、永不丢失的世界，而真实系统里成千上万条事务在并发争抢同一批数据，磁盘随时可能断电。如何在不牺牲正确性的前提下榨出吞吐，是这门学问的全部主题。</p>\n<p>四章按依赖顺序层层递进，每一章都建立在前一章的概念之上。</p>\n<p>第一章「基础」先把语言立起来。我们定义 ACID 四个字母各自的精确含义，列举并发会引入的脏读、不可重复读、幻读、写偏斜等异常，把 SQL 标准的四个隔离级别与这些异常一一对应，最后用可串行化理论给出「什么叫正确的并发调度」这一问题的数学答案——冲突图无环。没有这一章的词汇表，后面三章无从谈起。</p>\n<p>第二章「并发控制」回答「如何在运行时强制可串行化」。两阶段锁用加锁顺序保证冲突可串行化，代价是死锁；多版本并发控制让读不阻塞写、写不阻塞读，是今天 PostgreSQL、MySQL InnoDB 的主流引擎；乐观并发与时间戳排序则赌冲突很少、出错再回滚。三种思路各有适用场景，本章逐一拆解其机制与代价。</p>\n<p>第三章「恢复与持久性」守住 ACID 里的 A 与 D。预写日志确保已提交的修改即使崩溃也能重放回来，检查点与 ARIES 三阶段恢复让重启时间可控，缓冲区管理的刷盘策略决定了日志与数据页之间必须遵守的先后纪律。并发控制保证「并发不出错」，恢复机制保证「崩溃不丢数据」，二者合起来才是完整的事务。</p>\n<p>第四章「分布式事务」把前三章的单机结论搬到跨节点的世界，并展示它们如何被迫松动。两阶段提交用一个协调者把多节点的原子提交问题归约到共识；分布式快照隔离需要 TrueTime 或全局序列器来给跨分片事务排出一致顺序；Saga 干脆放弃原子性，用补偿事务换取在微服务架构下的最终一致性。从严格的 ACID 一路走到刻意放松的 BASE，这一章揭示了一致性与可用性之间永恒的权衡。</p>\n<p>读完四章，你应当能在拿到一个具体场景时判断：它需要哪一级隔离、用哪种并发控制、崩溃后怎么恢复、跨节点时该坚持强一致还是退守最终一致。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"acid-transactions","title":"事务与 ACID","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/foundations/acid-transactions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"anomalies-isolation-levels","title":"异常与隔离级别","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/foundations/anomalies-isolation-levels"},{"seq":3,"slug":"serializability-theory","title":"可串行化理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/foundations/serializability-theory"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"concurrency-control","title":"并发控制","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/concurrency-control","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"two-phase-locking","title":"两阶段锁与死锁","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/concurrency-control/two-phase-locking"},{"seq":2,"slug":"mvcc","title":"多版本并发控制 MVCC","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/concurrency-control/mvcc"},{"seq":3,"slug":"optimistic-timestamp","title":"乐观并发与时间戳排序","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/concurrency-control/optimistic-timestamp"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"recovery-durability","title":"恢复与持久性","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/recovery-durability","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"write-ahead-logging","title":"预写日志 WAL","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/recovery-durability/write-ahead-logging"},{"seq":2,"slug":"checkpoint-recovery","title":"检查点与崩溃恢复","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/recovery-durability/checkpoint-recovery"},{"seq":3,"slug":"buffer-management","title":"缓冲区与刷盘","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/recovery-durability/buffer-management"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"distributed","title":"分布式事务","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/distributed","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"two-phase-commit","title":"两阶段提交与共识","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/distributed/two-phase-commit"},{"seq":2,"slug":"distributed-isolation","title":"分布式快照隔离","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/distributed/distributed-isolation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"saga-patterns","title":"Saga 与最终一致性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/database-transactions-concurrency/distributed/saga-patterns"}]}]}